/**
 * German for the Vivre en France practice questions.
 *
 * The lessons of this course have read in German since v1.2.1053, quiz blocks
 * included. The practice bank behind them had no table at all, so the exam
 * screens went on asking in French. This is the same work as
 * ukQuestionBankTranslationsDe, for the French bank.
 *
 * Keyed on the FRENCH of frQuestionBank.ts, exactly as it stands there. Every
 * key was extracted from the built module and paired back by position, never
 * retyped: one wrong character — an apostrophe of the wrong kind, a missing
 * accent — and the lookup misses in silence, so the marker disappears and the
 * reader is told there is nothing for a question that was in fact translated.
 *
 * Names of laws, offices and institutions stay French, as they do in
 * VIVRE_EN_FRANCE_DE: la laïcité, le SMIC, le conseil de prud'hommes, la
 * carte Vitale. That is what the exam asks for. What is translated is the
 * explanation around them.
 *
 * Strings another German table already answers are deliberately absent. Every
 * table for one target is spread into a single object, so a second entry for
 * the same key would be a silent collision, and the older table would decide
 * the wording for both. check-fr-bank-translation counts what a reader
 * reaches rather than what this file holds.
 */
